{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והיה כל מבקש ה' יצא", :translit "vehayah kol mevakesh Hashem yetzei", :gloss "And it was, everyone who sought YHWH would go out"} {:he "מכאן שצריך אדם לגלות כדי שילמוד תורה", :translit "mikan shetsarikh adam legalot kedey sheyilmod Torah", :gloss "from here, that a person must go into exile, in order that he learn Torah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Derives the halakhic value of going into exile for Torah study from the word יצא (would go out)."}], :frame {:text "Rabbi Elazar states in the name of Rabbi Hanina: The exile atones for sin, and Resh Lakish adds that exile atones for everything. Going to a place of Torah is itself the exile. Rav Yehudah said: Always go to the place of Torah. Avimi says in the name of Rabbi Elazar: If one leaves from a place of Torah and returns, it is as though he departed from life. Rabbi Yohanan says: I learned the entire Torah only through the breaking of my body. Rabbi Nehorai teaches: Exile yourself to a place of Torah.", :sources ["b. Berakhot 63a" "b. Shabbat 147a" "b. Sanhedrin 37b" "m. Avot 4:14" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Vayissa 1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Derives the halakhic value of going into exile for Torah study from the word יצא (would go out).", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:20:51.124445261Z", :model "glm-5.2"}